== Relative file path == <!--T:70-->

<!--T:71-->
{{version|1.1}}

<!--T:72-->
It is possible to specify a relative path for the PAT file. For this the FreeCAD document must have been saved at least once. See [[Draft_ShapeString#Relative_file_path|Draft ShapeString]] for some examples.

== Notes == <!--T:53-->

<!--T:54-->
* For now the advice is to download a PAT file. Many can be found online. You can for example do a web search for {{FileName|acad.pat}} or {{FileName|acadiso.pat}}.
* A small PAT file is installed with FreeCAD: {{FileName|<program_folder>/data/Mod/TechDraw/PAT/FCPAT.pat}}, where {{FileName|<program_folder>}} is the FreeCAD program folder:
** On Linux it is usually {{FileName|/usr/share/freecad}}.
** On Windows it is usually {{FileName|C:\Program Files\FreeCAD}}.
** On macOS it is usually {{FileName|/Applications/FreeCAD}}.
* {{VersionMinus|1.0}}: Patterns with dashed lines are not handled properly.

== Properties == <!--T:59-->

<!--T:60-->
See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

<!--T:61-->
A Draft Hatch object is derived from a [[Part_Feature|Part Feature]] object and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional properties:

=== Data === <!--T:62-->

<!--T:63-->
{{TitleProperty|Hatch}}

<!--T:64-->
* {{Version|26.3}}: {{PropertyData|Faces|LinkSubList}}: specifies the objects and faces that are hatched. Replaces the {{PropertyData|Base}} property ({{VersionMinus|1.1}}).
* {{PropertyData|File|File}}: specifies the PAT file.
* {{PropertyData|Pattern|String}}: specifies the pattern name.
* {{PropertyData|Rotation|Angle}}: specifies the rotation of the pattern.
* {{PropertyData|Scale|Float}}: specifies the scale of the pattern.
* {{PropertyData|Translate|Bool}}: specifies if the faces are temporarily translated to the global XY-plane during the hatching process. Setting it to {{FALSE}} may give wrong results for non-XY faces.

== Scripting == <!--T:65-->

<!--T:66-->
See also: [https://freecad.github.io/SourceDoc/ Autogenerated API documentation] and [[FreeCAD_Scripting_Basics|FreeCAD Scripting Basics]].

<!--T:67-->
To create a Draft Hatch use the {{incode|make_hatch}} method of the Draft module.

</translate>
{{Code|code=
hatch = make_hatch(selection, filename, pattern, scale, rotation)
}}
<translate>

Where {{Incode|selection}} can be a single object, a list of objects, a selection set with subelements: {{Incode|Gui.Selection.getSelectionEx("", 0)}} , or a LinkSubList-like iterable.

<!--T:68-->
Example: 

</translate>
{{Code|code=
import FreeCAD as App
import Draft

doc = App.newDocument()

rectangle = Draft.make_rectangle(4000, 1000)
rectangle.MakeFace = True
filename = App.getResourceDir() + "Mod/TechDraw/PAT/FCPAT.pat"
pattern = "Horizontal5"
hatch_rectangle = Draft.make_hatch(rectangle, filename, pattern, scale=50, rotation=45)

box = doc.addObject("Part::Box")
box.Length = 2000
box.Width = 2000
box.Height = 2000
box.Placement.Base = App.Vector(5000, 0, 0)
hatch_box = Draft.make_hatch([[box, ["Face3", "Face6"]]], filename, pattern, scale=75, rotation=45)

doc.recompute()
}}
